## Summary

Fixes apostrophes being displayed as `&#39;` in the Files pane (both in the file name and the hover tooltip) on Windows with French locale.

The bug was introduced in commit bffbcf7451 (May 2025) when `LinkColumn.java` was refactored to use `SafeHtmlTemplates`. The template was using `value.asString()` which returns HTML-escaped text, then passing it as a String parameter which gets escaped again by the template:

```java
@Template("<div class=\"{0}\" title=\"{1}\">{1}</div>")
SafeHtml render(String className, String title);

// Called with:
sb.append(NAME_TEMPLATE.render(classNames, value.asString()));
```

## Fix

Use `SafeHtml` parameter directly, which renders entities correctly in both the title attribute and visible content:

```java
@Template("<div class=\"{0}\" title=\"{1}\">{1}</div>")
SafeHtml render(String className, SafeHtml value);

// Called with:
sb.append(NAME_TEMPLATE.render(classNames, value));
```

## Test plan

- [ ] Create a folder or file with an apostrophe in the name (e.g., "It's a test")
- [ ] Verify it displays correctly in the Files pane (not as `It&#39;s a test`)
- [ ] Verify the tooltip (title attribute) also shows correctly on hover

