This PR fixes an issue related to the most recent Copilot update. Newer version of Copilot require us to send an "initialized" notification before any other requests can be processed. However, we have code of the form:

```
if (ensureAgentRunning()) {
  sendRequest(...)
}
```

And while `ensureAgentRunning()` will enqueue the "initialized" notification if necessary, it doesn't ensure the request created via `sendRequest()` is appropriately sequenced after that request.

This fix seemed like the most straightforward:

- Before initialization has happened, process only the initialization-specific requests;
- After initialization, process requests in the queue in order.

